      "answer": "The approved live patch window for Verdant Bay is March 24, 2026, from 02:00 to 04:00 local time. If validation checks fail during the live patch, the rollback procedure is to run the command `orchestrator rollback --target ruleset=<prior_sha>`, which rehydrates the prior ruleset and replays the cache invalidation hook. After rollback, the steps include notifying Verdant Bay, opening an incident for manual remediation, and reverting any partial replays. The validation checks involve running 50 synthetic approval flows plus a sample of 50 in-flight approvals marked by the customer, but the exact criteria that trigger rollback are not detailed in the evidence. Detailed step-by-step instructions beyond the CLI command are also not provided. [art_fff67d92fe41, art_f893faeda15a]",
