      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were \"department\" and \"businessUnit.\" Merchant Services used \"businessUnit=merchant\" while Payments Ops used \"department=payments.\" This mismatch caused ingestion normalization to fail to collapse these into a single canonical attribute, which led to the Rules Engine failing to match on the entity tag used to route approvals [art_79f625aafa16].\n\nJin proposed a fast fix that involved adding a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest to map \"businessUnit\" to \"department\" (or vice versa) and publish a normalized field for the correlator. This fix is a configuration-only change that can be hot-reloaded, thus avoiding the need to wait for Okta change control, which would take 2\u20134 weeks [art_79f625aafa16].\n\nNo additional details on the exact configuration syntax of the preprocessing rule or the specific mapping rule code were provided in the evidence.",
