      "answer": "The customer most likely to defect to a cheaper tactical competitor if the next promised milestone is missed is Pioneer Freight Solutions. They are currently running a tactical PoC of NoiseGuard, a competitor product that is cheaper and offers quick tactical remediation. Procurement is likely to extend NoiseGuard and reduce Northstar's scope if milestones slip, indicating high retention risk.\n\nThe exact next promised milestone for Pioneer Freight Solutions is the verification of schema registry compatibility and collection of a taxonomy snapshot, due by 2026-03-22. This is the first milestone in the agreed remediation plan, which includes subsequent milestones such as shadow index build (2026-03-29 to 2026-04-09), backfill and index rebuild (2026-04-12 to 2026-04-30), and validation window (2026-05-01 to 2026-05-14).\n\nThe remediation plan includes a milestone-based SLA with a one-time credit of 10% of ACV if milestone acceptance is not met by agreed dates, reflecting the criticality of meeting these milestones to retain the customer. The key acceptance criteria for the milestone include precision@10 >= 0.8 for facility lookups, entity-link hit rate >= 90%, and incident grouping false-positive rate <= 5%.\n\nThe risk of missing milestones is explicitly linked to procurement pressure to extend the NoiseGuard PoC and reduce Northstar's scope, highlighting the competitive threat tied to milestone delivery [art_ac8afb52f2d3, art_7373b64fdfdd, art_a504e4c5b6f8].",
